 "beats": [
  {
   "type": "title",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "globe",
   "text": "So where exactly is the Strait of Hormuz?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "scene": "globe",
   "date": "Today",
   "place": "Strait of Hormuz",
   "text": "Right here. Between Iran and Oman, at the mouth of the Persian Gulf."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And why is everyone talking about it?",
   "scene": "gulfmap"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Well, think about oil. Almost every tanker leaving the Gulf has to pass through here. That's about one barrel in every five the world uses."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "strait",
   "date": "",
   "text": "Wow. How wide is it?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Hmm, about twenty-one miles at its narrowest. And the shipping lanes? Just two miles wide each way."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "poloroute",
   "text": "Was it always this important?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "date": "1272",
   "place": "Old Hormuz",
   "text": "Oh, long before oil. Back in 1272, Marco Polo passed through and saw ships from India unloading spices, pearls and silk."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "move",
   "date": "",
   "text": "Wait, the city was on the mainland back then?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Right. Then around 1300, to escape raiders, its rulers moved the whole city onto a bare island offshore."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "scene": "maokun",
   "date": "Early 1400s",
   "place": "Zheng He's voyages",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.7,
     0.5,
     1.3
    ]
   },
   "text": "A century later, Chinese treasure fleets anchored there too."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "ring",
   "date": "",
   "text": "Sounds like a pretty rich place."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "It was. People said: if all the world were a golden ring, Hormuz would be the jewel in it."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "albuquerque",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.3,
     1.3
    ]
   },
   "text": "Let me guess. Someone wanted that jewel."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "date": "September 1507",
   "place": "Hormuz",
   "text": "Good guess. In 1507, the Portuguese commander Afonso de Albuquerque arrived, burned the harbour's ships and forced the king to pay tribute."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "scene": "desert",
   "date": "",
   "text": "But here's the thing: three of his own captains sailed off, and he had to leave."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "fortress",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.45,
     1.3
    ]
   },
   "text": "So he gave up?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "date": "April 1515",
   "place": "Hormuz",
   "text": "Not at all. He came back in 1515 with twenty-seven ships, and Hormuz gave in."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "scene": "toll",
   "date": "",
   "text": "For about a century, ships between India, Persia and Arabia had to deal with Portuguese Hormuz."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "abbas",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.6,
     0.42,
     1.6
    ]
   },
   "text": "And nobody pushed back?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Well, Persia's Shah Abbas wanted it back. He had a great army. But he didn't have a navy."
  },
  {
   "type": "end",
   "text": "Part 2: the shah, the English and the oil",
   "sub": "Follow so you don't miss it"
  }
 ],
 "scene_pad": 0.5,
 "fade": 1.1
}